[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm trying to prove that the space of countable ordinals (minimal uncountable well-ordered set $\\omega_1$ )  under the order topology is first-countable.</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∣</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{\\alpha | \\alpha \\lt \\Omega \\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Ω</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Some books denote $\\omega_1$ or $\\Omega$<br>\nThis space is mentioned in mathlib's counterexample sections but it proves other properties and has no mention of countability axioms. I'm attempting to establish this result <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=JYWwDg9gTgLgBAWQIYwBYBtgCMBQB6AWgEI4BlAfUEngcgRjiQGd64YJJ0IBzYAYyXTgMwSHgFM4Ad2Bo40ACaioLNhA6cAnnAJ4cbUQDsyomLrAG4AeShzg%2B%2FqfMAVFWt79SwsThxpR0USCyIKKcSDTk8orkrOxc6uSiAI4RwaHhQiLiAFw4cHAAFJSAgQRwWZbWtvwAlHAAvHDFpfVY6rl5cFAAZujevv6BncBQDDAAwhAArvowSFjooikhYaVtAGJDI%2BNTM3OizrEaBaTGAHQAksAQBVY2dugnEKlIcDRVNVnNre1wPBD6I1AJjxWFA2nlbDAoFcAB5guCoJAAN3EqGhpTg0JOdAAPOVbvwHk8Xk0MScAExwhHI%2BG%2Fbbo%2FLHGDnS6k14nLbTWbzJpwvKjJAVO4nWmc3bkC4QCKdcjoGCLUIRfQo2HfBjQKDqIA\">here</a> where I used one pre-existing lemma. I tried searching the library but couldn't get lemma appropriate to reach the goal. Any help or strategy would be helpful thanks.</p>",
        "id": 628872652,
        "sender_full_name": "Sham S",
        "timestamp": 1791029673
    },
