    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"380294\">Matt Diamond</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/The.20space.20S_omega.20is.20first.20countable/near/628916190\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Did you have a proof in mind and you're just not sure how to implement it? Or are you not sure how the proof itself would go?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>i have the proof which is proving using (beta, x] intervals. Here if x is a limit ordinal we will have sequence rising to x (as they don't have immediate predecessor) and for isolated ordinals we have singletons which have immediate predecsor and the interval becomes just {x}. This way its easier to implement in lean I guess. I needed help with the implementation. Apologies as my question was unclear with the kind of help/suggestions required</p>",
